## Fonts

The pages load **Inter** and **Wix Madefor Display** from Google Fonts at runtime. Both
are licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1; no font binaries are committed to this
repository or emitted into the site build.

VitePress self-hosts its own copy of Inter for the documentation theme. That copy ships
with the `vitepress` package under the same OFL terms.

Font binaries are deliberately kept out of this repository and out of the site build.
Trial and evaluation builds of commercial typefaces, in particular, permit neither web
embedding nor redistribution, and a licensed face is easy to add without noticing. So
`tests/integration/build-output.test.ts` fails the build if a font binary appears in the
Next.js output at all — add a face by loading it from a host whose licence allows it, not
by committing the file.
